## Multimodal AI Meaning: What Does It Actually Mean?

**Multimodal AI** is any AI system that can process and integrate information from more than one type of data — or "modality." IBM defines it as machine learning models capable of handling **text, images, audio, and video** in combination, rather than treating each as a separate problem.

### How It Differs from Traditional (Unimodal) AI

| Feature | Unimodal AI | Multimodal AI |
|---|---|---|
| Input types | One (e.g., text only) | Multiple (text + image + audio + video) |
| Understanding | Narrow, single-channel | Contextual, cross-channel |
| Example | GPT-2 (text only) | GPT-4o (text, image, audio) |
| Real-world fit | Limited | Mirrors how humans actually communicate |

---

## How Multimodal AI Works (Under the Hood)

Multimodal AI models follow a three-stage pipeline: **encode → fuse → decode.**
1. **Early Fusion:** Token-level joint sequence processing.
2. **Intermediate Fusion:** Cross-attention adapters between dedicated ViT/Audio encoders and central LLM.
3. **Late Fusion:** Decision-level ensembling.

